# Never cache the SPA-fallback HTML, so every visitor always gets an
# index.html that references the current (hashed) JS/CSS chunk names.
# Prevents "Failed to load module script ... MIME type text/html" after
# a new deploy, where a cached HTML shell points at chunk hashes that
# no longer exist.
#
# IMPORTANT: this must be a catch-all (/*), not just /index.html and /.
# Cloudflare Pages serves index.html via SPA fallback for EVERY unmatched
# path — /auth/callback, /dashboard, /journal/trades, etc. — not only the
# literal root. A hard navigation to any of those (e.g. the full-page
# redirect an OAuth login performs to /auth/callback) happens before
# Angular's router even exists, so a stale cached shell for one of those
# paths fails at the very first <script type="module"> tag, with nothing
# yet running client-side to recover from it. Only /index.html and / were
# covered before, leaving every other route exposed to exactly that.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Hashed build assets are content-addressed (name changes when content
# changes), so they're safe to cache forever. Cloudflare Pages merges
# per-path header rules, so these override the /* no-cache above for
# anything matching *.js / *.css specifically.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
